[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"758","stub":{"id":"758","section":"2. Bragg's Bay to Pontook","altname":"","river":"Androscoggin","difficulty":"ItoII","states":["USA-NHM"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"1040","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":null,"id":"108787","location":{"latitude":"44.7789001464844","longitude":"-71.1351013183594"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":null,"id":"114022","location":{"latitude":"44.6338996887207","longitude":"-71.2497024536133"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"17","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[],"detail":{"id":"758","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"This is a good novice/touring river. Mostly quickwater with an occasional easy rapid. Good area to see moose, eagles and other wildlife. The river parallels the road all the way so there are many other putin and takeout oppertunities along the way. The farther down the river one travels the more sluggish the flow especially after passing 7 Islands Bridge. Mollidgewock Campground, located about 4 miles downriver from Errol, provides a great stop-off or base for running this section of the Androscoggin.\n\nCheck out the [Androscoggin River Watershed Council](http://www.avcnet.org/arwc/recreationintro.html) for more information on this river.\n\n## Erroll NH...Gateway town\n\nErrol, NH, located in northern NH close to the Maine border, offers a wide range of boating opportunities all summer long. This area offers some of the most remote regions in the eastern US. Wildlife is plentiful and may include moose, bear, loons, bald eagles etc. In addition, Lake Umbagog, located just north of Errol, is a federally protected [National Wildlife Refuge](http://lakeumbagog.fws.gov/).\n\nThe [Errol rapid](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/3736/%20) located on the east side of Errol is a short class-II section good for training and novices. Saco Bound (Northern Waters) has set up a small outfit here on the western shore with a campground, paddling school, and small boating shop. Water is controlled by a hydro dam just upstream from the campground and runs through this section every summer day. This section is onlabout 1/3 of a mile long and boaters usually carry back upstream and run it several times a day.\n\nThe [Pontook](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/3686/%20) section of the Androscoggin is about 15 miles south of Errol on Route 16. This section offers a longer and more interesting class II run. Pontook dam releases most weekends.\n\nStarting in late June and ending in late August, the Magalloway and Rapid rivers offer more challenging boating.\n\nThe [Magalloway](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/824/), located 20 miles north of Errol in Wilson Mills Maine, offers class III and V boating on the upper stretch. Releases are on weekends starting in late June through the second week in July. The Rapid then has four release weekends until the middle of August then once again the Magalloway finishes up the month of August with weekend releases.\n\nThe [Rapid](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/881/) River offers class IV boating in a remote setting. The Rapid can only be reached via a maze of logging roads just outside of Upton Maine about 10 miles east of Errol.\n\n**Campgrounds / Lodging /Rafting**\n\nErrol Motel, Main St, Errol, NH 03579, (603-482-3256)\n\n[Northern Waters (Saco Bound)](http://www.sacobound.com/kayak.html), Kayaking school, camping, excursions, paddling shop. Phone: 603.447.2177\n\nMagalloway River Inn, Route 16, Errol, NH 03579, (603-482-9883)\n\nAziscohos Valley Camping Area, Route 16 Wilson Mills Maine (207-486-3271)\n\n[Mollidgewock State Park Campground](http://www.nhparks.state.nh.us/ParksPages/Mollidgewock/MollidgewockCmp.html), Route 16 Errol, NH Phone: 603-482-3373 Reservations: 603-271-3628\n\n[Lakewood Camps](http://www.lakewoodcamps.com/): 207.243.2959\n\n[Log Haven Campground](http://www.loghaven.com/): 603.482.3294\n\n[Umbagog Outfitters](http://www.umbout.com/%20) P.O. Box 268 Errol, NH 03579 phone: 603-356-3292\n\n**Food**\n\nThe Northern Exposure: Main St Errol, NH, 03579, (603) 482-3852\n\nErrol Cream Barrel & Chuck Wagon 482-3258 Main Street, Errol NH 03579","averageGradient":"5","maxGradient":"12","length":"17.5","correlations":[{"reachID":"758","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"750","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"10000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"Androscoggin River at Errol, NH","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"01053500","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"1040","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.77","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"44.7825","longitude":"-71.1286111"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/01053500","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/01053500/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geological Survey"}}},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"migration-runnable","latestReading":{"value":"1040","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null}}],"pointOfInterestIDs":["108787","114022"],"geometry":{"type":"LineString","coordinates":[[-71.1352838313031,44.7778331324264],[-71.13424786669236,44.77765593049